course: dictionary
lesson: 4700
title: Meet the honeybee
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A honeybee is a bee that lives in a large group called a colony. Its colony makes honey and wax, and every bee in the colony has a job. Look for clues in the words around the bee to understand what it does.
explain: «On a sunny day a honeybee lands on a flower, drinks sweet nectar with its long tongue and flies off with yellow balls of pollen packed on its back legs, like a shopper with two full bags.» The sentence tells you the honeybee collects food from flowers, and the shopper comparison helps you picture the pollen.
explain: «A honeybee leaves its barbed stinger in the skin and dies after stinging.» Barbed means it has tiny hooks, like a fish hook, so the sting stays in your skin. If a honeybee comes near you, stay calm and walk away slowly.
fact: A honeybee is an insect with six legs, wings and a body in three parts.
fact: A honeybee colony has one queen, many female workers and some male drones.
fact: Honeybees collect nectar and pollen from flowers, and this pollinates plants so they can make fruit and seeds.
fact: A honeybee can sting once and then dies, because its barbed sting stays in the skin.
exercise: «A honeybee lands on a flower and drinks sweet nectar with its long tongue.» What does a honeybee drink from a flower? | Pollen | Petals | *Nectar | Wax
exercise: A honeybee lives in a large group called a what? | *Colony | Pack | Flock | Herd
exercise: «A honeybee leaves its barbed stinger in the skin and dies after stinging.» What happens to the honeybee after it stings? | It flies away and lives for years | It turns into a wasp | *It dies | It makes honey
test: What does a honeybee colony make? | *Honey and wax | Sugar cubes | Milk | Silk
test: What should you do if a honeybee comes close to you? | Run and shout loudly | Swat it quickly with your hands | Pick it up gently | *Stay calm and walk away slowly
exam: Why does a honeybee's sting get stuck in your skin? | It does not get stuck at all | *Because it has tiny barbs, like a fish hook | Because the bee likes your skin | Because it is made of glue
